{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963527-corax-rules-w20","id":963527,"title":"Corax rules (W20)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-04T21:27:16-07:00","id":963527,"title":"Corax rules (W20)","content":"Hi there!<br /> <br /> I just read the corax section of the W20 changing needs book and I've a few questions, not covered there:<br /> <br /> -Do they pass to the umbra like the garou?<br /> -Can they spend rage for extra actions like garou? Or for other benefits, like gourahl?<br /> -How do they recover rage?<br /> -How do they recover gnosis?<br /> -can they frenzy?<br /> <br /> <br /> Fetish egg related questions:<br /> -can it be placed on any human or crow? Or does it need to be place on a kinfolk?<br /> -does it need to be placed on the subject the same time it is born out can it be placed at any time during the subject's life?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T21:43:45-07:00","id":963538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>erSito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963527-corax-rules-w20#post963527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there!<br /> <br /> I just read the corax section of the W20 changing needs book and I've a few questions, not covered there:<br /> <br /> -Do they pass to the umbra like the garou?<br /> -Can they spend rage for extra actions like garou? Or for other benefits, like gourahl?<br /> -How do they recover rage?<br /> -How do they recover gnosis?<br /> -can they frenzy?<br /> <br /> <br /> Fetish egg related questions:<br /> -can it be placed on any human or crow? Or does it need to be place on a kinfolk?<br /> -does it need to be placed on the subject the same time it is born out can it be placed at any time during the subject's life?<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes to the whole first block. Rage and gnosis recovered the same.<br /> Needs to be kinfolk. Any time on their life should do.<br /> Sorry for short answers, I'm on my phone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T22:10:23-07:00","id":963549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963527-corax-rules-w20?p=963538#post963538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Needs to be kinfolk. Any time on their life should do.</div> </div> </div> </div>It technically doesn't need to be, but skipping over kin is a social no-no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T22:15:31-07:00","id":963552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>erSito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963527-corax-rules-w20#post963527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there!<br /> <br /> -can it be placed on any human or crow? Or does it need to be place on a kinfolk?<br /> -does it need to be placed on the subject the same time it is born out can it be placed at any time during the subject's life?<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically....raven, not crow<br /> <br /> Last I was aware the fetish egg had to be at time of birth because it was supposed to be a slow mingling of raven and human. Its the rushed merging in the case of Buzzards (Book of the Wyrm) that makes them not quite right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T22:44:25-07:00","id":963560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963527-corax-rules-w20?p=963549#post963549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It technically doesn't need to be, but skipping over kin is a social no-no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Wasn't aware of that. Seems very odd. Thanks for the correction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T23:42:25-07:00","id":963575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963527-corax-rules-w20?p=963538#post963538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes to the whole first block. Rage and gnosis recovered the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they recover rage the first time the see the moon every day? Or is seeing the sun?<br /> Do they recover the amount of rage according to the phase of the moon, but never &quot;all&quot; because they don't have any auspice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T06:46:53-07:00","id":963669,"title":"","content":"And you have to cross breeds. A corvid can only adopt human children while a homids can only adopt bird children. That factor has kept the Corax more unified than other Changing Breeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T08:06:05-07:00","id":963695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>erSito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963527-corax-rules-w20?p=963575#post963575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do they recover rage the first time the see the moon every day? Or is seeing the sun?<br /> Do they recover the amount of rage according to the phase of the moon, but never &quot;all&quot; because they don't have any auspice?</div> </div> </div> </div>So this they don't address, as far as I know.<br /> <br /> Personally, I generally rule it the first time they look up to the sun, and give them an amount of rage proportional to the time of day, with midday (theoretically when the sun is highest) being 4. I also never have them just fill &quot;all&quot; since like you said, they don't have auspices. But yea, this is definitely houserule territory.<br /> <br /> It is also entirely possible that they just don't have access to this means of Rage recovery since they aren't Gaia's warriors, and so shouldn't need as much Rage. I obviously dislike approaching from this angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T08:15:37-07:00","id":963698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963527-corax-rules-w20?p=963695#post963695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So this they don't address, as far as I know.<br /> <br /> Personally, I generally rule it the first time they look up to the sun, and give them an amount of rage proportional to the time of day, with midday (theoretically when the sun is highest) being 4. I also never have them just fill &quot;all&quot; since like you said, they don't have auspices. But yea, this is definitely houserule territory.<br /> <br /> It is also entirely possible that they just don't have access to this means of Rage recovery since they aren't Gaia's warriors, and so shouldn't need as much Rage. I obviously dislike approaching from this angle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is where I leaned on the Mokole breed book. I feel like the mokole book answers a lot of questions for the Corax that their own breed book didn't when it comes to being a solar shifter vs a lunar one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T08:23:30-07:00","id":963702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963527-corax-rules-w20?p=963698#post963698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is where I leaned on the Mokole breed book. I feel like the mokole book answers a lot of questions for the Corax that their own breed book didn't when it comes to being a solar shifter vs a lunar one.</div> </div> </div> </div>So how does it work for the Mokole then?<br /> I know I could dig out my books and look it up, but I'm assuming you know off the top of your head <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T08:29:38-07:00","id":963705,"title":"","content":"Mokole (and in my games Corax) regain Rage and have their frenzy diff's adjusted based on how sunny it is. So basically at night or cut off from windows they get 0 Rage back and (in my games, as W20 changed the frenzy rules for simplicity) its a diff 8 to Rage rolls...then they regain 1 Rage if its really cloudy or they are inside.<br /> If its foggy or light cloud cover regain 2, if the sun is dim (like sun set or sun rise) Rage 3, if its a bright day out 4, and high noon no clouds 5. Mokole get the added benifit of auspices (granted the Crowned is so screwed on that one) and the Corax have no auspices so I guess they don't really get a complete refill option but ...how many Corax are really running around with 6+ Rage?<br /> <br /> There is a bunch of optional stuff in the Mokole book that I do play with, like Sunbane (Helios punishing fallen Mokole and Corax) and how Mokole blood (and in my games Corax blood too) can induce torpor in a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 09-05-2016, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T08:42:28-07:00","id":963714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/963527-corax-rules-w20?p=963705#post963705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mokole (and in my games Corax) regain Rage and have their frenzy diff's adjusted based on how sunny it is. So basically at night or cut off from windows they get 0 Rage back and (in my games, as W20 changed the frenzy rules for simplicity) its a diff 8 to Rage rolls...then they regain 1 Rage if its really cloudy or they are inside.<br /> If its foggy or light cloud cover regain 2, if the sun is dim (like sun set or sun rise) Rage 3, if its a bright day out 4, and high noon no clouds 5. Mokole get the added benifit of auspices (granted the Crowned is so screwed on that one) and the Corax have no auspices so I guess they don't really get a complete refill option but ...how many Corax are really running around with 6+ Rage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. Yea, I didn't remember offhand and figured that would be helpful to the OP.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}